{"action":"final","query":{"op":"none","scope":null,"id":null,"text":null,"start":null,"end":null,"offset":null,"derived_op":null,"groupBy":null},"diagnosis":"scalar_constant treats every value equal to zero as a null constant. Python considers -0.0 equal to 0, so this discards its floating-point sign. The failing float32 observation contains 32 positive-zero bit patterns (0x00000000) where negative zero (0x80000000) is required; the positive-zero control passes all 32 elements. Restrict the null shortcut to non-floating types so floating zeros use the existing typed constant constructors (and existing FP8 conversion path). Nonzero construction remains unchanged. Compilation and post-patch device results are unavailable; float16, bfloat16, and float64 behavior has not been observed in the supplied evidence.","locations":[{"source_id":"source-06","start_line":601,"end_line":623}],"citations":[{"case_id":"negative-zero-00","evidence_ids":["observation-negative-zero-00"]},{"case_id":"negative-zero-01","evidence_ids":["observation-negative-zero-01"]}],"edits":[{"source_id":"source-06","old":"        if value == 0:
